findings.repair:
Separate into three phases: (1) validate every qty in a first pass, raising ValueError before any mutation; (2) aggregate required quantities per SKU and verify every SKU exists and has sufficient aggregate stock, returning False without touching stock; (3) only then deduct. Example replacement:

    def reserve(stock, requests):
        for sku, qty in requests:
            if type(qty) is not int or qty <= 0:
                raise ValueError('quantity')
        agg = {}
        for sku, qty in requests:
            agg[sku] = agg.get(sku, 0) + qty
        for sku, need in agg.items():
            if sku not in stock or stock[sku] < need:
                return False
        for sku, need in agg.items():
            stock[sku] -= need
        return True
